IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-drafting`

-- Tests of lga-drafting.l4 (sections 16, 17 and 19).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text; the provision and the reading are named beside each group.


§§ `s 16 (text lines 690 to 701)`

#ASSERT `s 16(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to promote the legal effectiveness, clarity and intelligibility of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments`
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` `undertaking or supervising the drafting of legislative instruments and notifiable instruments` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` `scrutinising preliminary drafts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` `providing advice concerning the drafting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` `providing training in drafting and related matters to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` `arranging the temporary secondment of APS employees in the Office of Parliamentary Counsel to Departments or other agencies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` `providing drafting precedents to officers and employees of Departments or other agencies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the steps referred to in subsection (1) may include the step` `any other step` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16(3)(a): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to prevent gender-specific language where it is not necessary to identify persons by their sex`
#ASSERT `s 16(3)(b): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to advise the rule-maker` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(3)(b): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to advise the rule-maker` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16(3)(b): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to advise the rule-maker` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16(3)(b): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to advise the rule-maker` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16(3)(c): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to notify both Houses of the Parliament` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(3)(c): the First Parliamentary Counsel must cause steps to be taken to notify both Houses of the Parliament` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 17 and 19 (text lines 703 to 712)`

#ASSERT `s 17(1): the rule-maker must be satisfied that the consultation the rule-maker considers appropriate, and that is reasonably practicable, has been undertaken` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(1): the rule-maker must be satisfied that the consultation the rule-maker considers appropriate, and that is reasonably practicable, has been undertaken` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(1): the rule-maker must be satisfied that the consultation the rule-maker considers appropriate, and that is reasonably practicable, has been undertaken` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(1): the rule-maker must be satisfied that the consultation the rule-maker considers appropriate, and that is reasonably practicable, has been undertaken` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(2): the rule-maker may have regard to the matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2): the rule-maker may have regard to the matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(3): the consultation could involve the notification` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(3): the consultation could involve the notification` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19: the failure to consult affects the validity or enforceability of the legislative instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19: the failure to consult affects the validity or enforceability of the legislative instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
